# Secrets.
#
# `.env` matches that exact name only, so the three rules below would let a
# *backup* of it through: `.env.bak`, `.env.ci-bak`, `.env.2026-08-30` are all
# unmatched, all full of live keys, and all swept up by a single `git add -A`.
# That is not hypothetical - a tooling step moved `.env` aside mid-session and
# left exactly such a file sitting untracked in the repo root.
#
# `.env.*` closes it, and `!.env.example` keeps the one file that must ship.
# Add a further negation if another `.env.<something>` ever needs committing;
# do not widen the rule.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Python environments and bytecode
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
lib/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.DS_Store

# Test, lint and type-check caches. pyproject.toml configures pytest, and a
# contributor may reasonably run ruff or mypy even though this repo pins
# neither.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/

# Coverage output
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Node, if anyone runs npm from the repo root rather than frontend/
node_modules/

# Editor and IDE directories. `.vscode/extensions.json` is committed as a
# workspace recommendation (see frontend/.vscode/), so it is excepted.
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp

# Run artifacts - regenerated every run, never committed
# `.playwright-mcp/` is written by the Playwright MCP browser tools (page
# snapshots, console dumps, screenshots) wherever they are invoked from.
.playwright-mcp/
output/
*.png
*.log

# Local databases. The service defaults to output/validator-studio.db, which
# the rule above already covers; these catch a DATABASE_URL pointed elsewhere.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# CrewAI local state. tokens.enc is the AMP tracing credential: it is a
# secret, it expires, and it must never reach an image or a repo.
.checkpoints/
tokens.enc
db/

# Vendored CrewAI agent skills, installed by `npx skills add crewaiinc/skills`.
# COMMITTED deliberately, not ignored - they make the repo self-describing for
# any coding agent that opens it (Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI and 12 others read
# .agents/skills; Claude Code reads .claude/skills). Re-install with the same
# command to update. Listed here only so the decision is visible:
#   .agents/skills/    <- kept
#   .claude/skills/    <- kept
#
# uv.lock is also committed - 07-deployment.md requires it at the repo root,
# because Render auto-detects it to pin the build.

# The global *.png rule above is for run artifacts (plot output, screenshots).
# Frontend source assets are real code and must survive a fresh clone.
# The one file this currently rescues is hero.png, which
# frontend/src/components/HelloWorld.vue imports - and this comment used to say
# "at build time", which is not true: HelloWorld.vue has no importers anywhere
# (`grep -rn HelloWorld frontend/src` is empty), so it never enters Vite's
# module graph and hero.png is never emitted into a bundle. The exception is
# kept anyway, because remaining-work item 7 is an open keep-or-delete decision
# about that whole dead cluster and an ignore rule must not decide it silently.
!frontend/src/assets/**/*.png

# VISUAL BASELINES, which are the opposite of a run artifact.
#
# A screenshot Playwright WROTE during a run is disposable; a screenshot it
# COMPARES against is the assertion itself, and one that is not committed cannot
# fail. Before 2026-09-04 the global `*.png` rule swallowed both, so
# `run-canvas.spec.ts` had three baselines that existed on one machine and
# nowhere else - which means a fresh clone generated them on its first run and
# passed, whatever the canvas looked like.
#
# The `-<project>-<platform>` suffix Playwright appends is why this is safe:
# a Linux run looks for `-linux` files, finds none and writes its own rather
# than diffing against a Windows render of the same page.
!frontend/e2e/visual/**/*.png

# RUN-SHELL EVIDENCE, which is neither a run artifact nor a baseline.
#
# `docs/run-shell/DEFINITION-OF-DONE.md` is binding only if a reader who has
# not seen the build conversation can execute every check in it and reach the
# same verdict - and half its rows are answered by a screenshot at a named
# path, read by a cold reader who is given the PNGs and nothing else. A
# captured-and-then-ignored screenshot cannot answer anything: it exists on one
# machine, the verdict table cites a path that is empty on a fresh clone, and
# the criterion silently becomes an assertion by the builder, which §0 says is
# never evidence.
#
# Scoped to that one directory rather than to `docs/**`, because the global
# rule above is right about everything else: a plot or a stray capture written
# somewhere in `docs/` is still disposable.
!docs/run-shell/evidence/**/*.png

# Lecture source material - 20 MB binary, not application source.
*.pdf

# Plan 08 C11: a user's own SKILL.md packs are materialised here as a CACHE of
# the `user_skills` rows. The committed half is `data/skills/builtin/`, which
# is this repository's own four and is NOT ignored.
data/skills/users/
